%S A399721 2,4,1,3,10,12,4,6,18,5,7,9,26,8,10,32,34,11,13,40,12,14,46,48,15,17,
%T A399721 54,16,18,20,62,19,21,68,70,22,24,76,23,25,27,84,26,28,90,92,29,31,98,
%U A399721 30,32,104,106,33,35,112,34,36,38,120,37,39,126,128,40,42,134,41,43
%N A399721 The map of the "Lucas-Collatz" function: if n is Lucas-odd (A399306), then a(n)=2*n; if n is Lucas-even (A399305), then a(n) is the integer whose minimal Lucas representation (A130310) results from removing the final 0 of A130310(n).
%C A399721 Conjecture: Under repeated iteration of this function, the orbit of every positive integer that is not a multiple of 5 reaches either the cycle 2, 4, 3, 1, 2 or the long cycle of 23 (A399307), and the orbit of every positive multiple of 5 reaches either the cycle 5, 10, 5 or the long cycle of 70 (A399308).
%e A399721 a(1) = 2 since 1 is Lucas-even and removing the final 0 of A130310(1) = 10 results in A130310(2) = 1.
%e A399721 a(2) = 4 = 2*2 since 2 is Lucas-odd because A130310(2) = 1 does not end in a 0.
%e A399721 a(5) = 10 = 2*5 since 5 is Lucas-odd because removing the final 0 of A130310(5) = 1010 does not result in a valid minimal Lucas representation of another integer.
%e A399721 a(12) = 9 since 12 is Lucas-even and removing the final 0 of A130310(12) = 100010 results in A130310(9) = 10001.
%e A399721 a(14) = 8 since 14 is Lucas-even and removing the final 0 of A130310(14) = 100100 results in A130310(8) = 10010.
%e A399721 a(16) = 32 = 2*16 since 16 is Lucas-odd because removing the final 0 of A130310(16) = 101010 does not result in a valid minimal Lucas representation of another integer.
%e A399721 a(19) = 13 since 19 is Lucas-even and removing the final 0 of A130310(19) = 1000010 results in A130310(13) = 100001.
%e A399721 a(23) = 46 = 2*23 since 23 is Lucas-odd because removing the final 0 of A130310(23) = 1001010 does not result in a valid minimal Lucas representation of another integer.
%Y A399721 Cf. A399305, A399306, A399307, A399308, A130310, A000032, A006370.
%K A399721 nonn,new
%O A399721 1,1
